; THROWAWAY — BUG-0003 §V.2 / WO-0063 §10. This directory belongs at
; test/bug3_probe/ on the TRANSIENT tree only, and is deleted with that tree.
; It is never committed to the working branch: PROTOCOL §10's transient model
; governs the whole operation (apply, run, harvest, revert fully, nothing
; enters history), and WO-0063 §10.1 places this artefact outside the row
; denominator, the unit inventory and every campaign scorecard.
;
; The probe is an executable on the runtest alias rather than an expect test,
; for test/cost_probe/'s reason: its result is a measurement of a design nobody
; intends to keep, and a measurement can never be promoted into a snapshot —
; the build workflow's `git diff --cached --exit-code` step would then be
; diffing a pre-fix module's behaviour into the tree forever. The output goes
; to the CI log instead, every line prefixed BUG3-PROBE so it greps out.
;
; (deps (universe)) disables dune's cache for this action. Without it a cache
; hit on an unchanged executable could replay a stale figure, which for a
; severity decision is worse than no figure at all.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; OPERATOR NOTE — read this before running, it is the one way to get no output
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; On the transient tree the module under test carries fafb83d's PRE-FIX
; content, so the committed M03 suite is EXPECTED TO BE RED there — that is the
; whole premise of the measurement (BUG-0002 and BUG-0003 were both open at
; that SHA). Dune stops scheduling new actions after a failure unless told
; otherwise, so a plain `dune runtest` may never reach this rule.
;
; Prefer either of these, which do not depend on the rest of the suite:
;
;     dune exec test/bug3_probe/bug3_severity_probe.exe
;     dune build @bug3-probe
;
; or, if running the whole alias, pass --keep-going:
;
;     dune runtest --keep-going
;
; The two rules below are deliberate duplication: the runtest attachment is the
; cost_probe precedent, and the named alias is the insurance that the operator
; gets the numbers even when everything around them is failing. Running both in
; one invocation simply prints the block twice — the probe is print-only and has
; no state, so a double run costs a duplicated log block and nothing else.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Libraries: exactly test/cosim/dune's list. This probe links NO test library —
; not test_xgmii_rx_64, not any family module — so it pulls no expect tests into
; its executable and cannot be perturbed by the suite's own redness. It reaches
; the DUT the way test/cosim/ours_run.ml does, through the published
; Cyclesim.With_interface entry point and field-name projection, and it reads
; nothing under libs/ or rtl_snapshots/ (PROTOCOL §10).
;
; No (preprocess ...) stanza: the probe uses no ppx. It defines no Hardcaml
; interface of its own (it uses Xgmii_rx_64.I / .O, already derived in the
; library) and contains no let%expect_test — which is also why
; tools/dv_checks.sh's repository-wide `let%expect_test` inventory is unchanged
; by this directory's presence, and why tools/precompile_check.sh auto-classes
; it EXCLUDED ("executable stanza; this harness compiles libraries only")
; without needing an entry added to either script.

(executable
 (name bug3_severity_probe)
 (modules bug3_severity_probe)
 (libraries
  hardcaml
  hardcaml_ethernet
  dv_xgmii
  dv_xgmii_probe
  dv_axi64_probe
  dv_monitors))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (universe))
 (action
  (run %{exe:bug3_severity_probe.exe})))

(rule
 (alias bug3-probe)
 (deps
  (universe))
 (action
  (run %{exe:bug3_severity_probe.exe})))
